203
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:05,800
And they brought it to our prayer team a few months ago?

204
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,800
Yeah.

205
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:07,800
About a month and a half.

206
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:08,800
About a month and a half ago.

207
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:16,800
And our prayer team prayed over this blanket and prayed for healing and prayed for the kingdom of God to be breaking into the world through this act of sacrificial love.

208
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:25,800
And the person came back today and said that as far as we can tell, the cancer is gone.

209
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:30,800
And we hear stories like that.

210
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:37,800
And the person who had the story immediately picked up his phone and called his friend who helped him pray for the blanket who isn't here and says, "Are you going to church this morning?"

211
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:38,800
And the guy's like, "Yeah."

212
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:41,800
And he's like, "Well, I got something for you to praise Jesus about this morning."

213
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:46,800
We need to fix our eyes on what is praiseworthy and excellent and good.

214
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:55,800
We need to remind ourselves that even in the brokenness of this world, with the sorrow and pain of sin-marred creation, that God is doing something.

215
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,800
Amen.

216
00:20:56,800 --> 00:21:02,800
That his kingdom is coming and that his will will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

217
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:14,800
The example of Christ isn't to form a Christian community that is shallow or ignores the realities of a broken world, but it chooses to celebrate where God is at work.

218
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:19,800
As followers of Christ, we should be full of joy, shining a light of hope to a dark world.

219
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:24,800
We need each other to do this because again, 85% negative, 95% repetitive.

220
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:29,800
We need each other to get out of this cycle.

221
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:33,800
We need to share testimonies of what God has done in our life.

222
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:38,800
We need to point out the ways in which we see God is at work in others.

223
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,800
And this is not easy.

224
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:44,800
Many of us have never been, this has never been modeled for us, right?

225
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:54,800
Many of us have only ever existed in Christian communities where it was shallow, where we talked about whatever everybody else was talking about, the weather and whatever else.

226
00:21:54,800 --> 00:22:01,800
And so if you've never, if it's never been modeled to you, this will feel awkward getting real with people.

227
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:07,800
I've been working towards this with a small community of people and it gets weird.

228
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:11,800
A dude kissed me on the neck not too long ago, right?

229
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:14,800
And I'm like, I don't know how I feel about this.

230
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:18,800
It gets real.

231
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:19,800
It gets weird.

232
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:22,800
But it's beautiful.

233
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,800
It's family around the table.

234
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:27,800
So it's never been modeled for us.

235
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:28,800
Life is hectic.

236
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:31,800
Sometimes, sometimes we're moving so fast that we don't even know how we feel.

237
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:32,800
Rightness.

238
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:33,800
Rightness.

239
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:43,800
And so then the thought of being able to share with somebody else what we feel is really difficult.

240
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:47,800
This is why these spiritual practices build off of each other, right?

241
00:22:47,800 --> 00:23:03,800
Because if you're practicing solitude on a somewhat regular basis or Sabbath, where you're breaking away from the business of the world and the noise of life, then you're able to, when you come to the table, you're able to bring more of yourself because you're in touch with yourself and with God.

242
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:05,800
You can be present to yourself and to God.

243
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:08,800
Some things build off one another.

244
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:14,800
Some of you can't struggle with this idea because vulnerability has been taken advantage in the past.

245
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:17,800
You've shared your joys and your sorrows.

246
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:23,800
And that person that you've shared it with has used and abused or manipulated that information.

247
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:28,800
And so I'm, I'm, I'm, I'm, I'm sympathetic to that.

248
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:31,800
And I, I realized that for many of us, this will take a long time.

249
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:34,800
It'll be a slow process.

250
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:38,800
But I think the alternative is far more painful.

251
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:48,800
Being alone and isolated and keeping ourselves walled off to the community around us is, is worse than, than not.

252
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:50,800
All right.

253
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:58,800
Jesus isn't just a celebrator of God's goodness on earth as it is in heaven, but he is also a mourner of the way that sin has broken good creation.

254
00:23:58,800 --> 00:24:02,800
Going further down in Mark chapter 14, starting at verse 32.

255
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:14,800
After they celebrated this meal of defiant joy in the midst of one of the hardest situations in human history, Jesus goes to a place called Gethsemane.

256
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:17,800
And he said to his disciples, Sit here while I pray.

257
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,800
He took Peter, James and John along with them.

258
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:22,800
And he began to be deeply distressed and troubled.

259
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:26,800
My soul is overwhelmed with sorrow to the point of death.

260
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:30,800
He said them, Stay here and keep watch.

261
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:39,800
Going a little further, he fell on the ground and he prayed, if possible, the hour, that if possible, the hour might pass for him.

262
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:42,800
Abba, Father, he said, everything is possible for you.

263
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:44,800
Take this cup from me.

264
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:47,800
Yet not what I will, but what you will.

265
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:53,800
This is the same night, right?

266
00:24:53,800 --> 00:25:02,800
They move from this table of celebrating God's deliverance from Egypt's slavery in the past of the Passover lamb.

267
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:09,800
And they move towards this place of somber prayer, mourning the brokenness.

268
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:18,800
He's fully aware that the result of sin and death is that he's going to have to face the result of sin and death face to face within the next 24 hours.

269
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:24,800
And so he invites his disciples to join him in prayer rooted in his suffering.

270
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:29,800
And he invites his closest followers even further into the suffering and pain.

271
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:34,800
Joy is something that we could probably celebrate with all of our community.

272
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:39,800
But sorrow is often reserved for those even closest to us.

273
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:48,800
Jesus invites his closest three into a vulnerable, deep place of pain reserved for his closest community.

274
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:51,800
This is why I'm preaching on this for four weeks.

275
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:59,800
Because you have to do the work to develop the close-knit community before suffering happens.

276
00:25:59,800 --> 00:26:06,800
Because suffering hits and we look around for the people that we're going to go to war with in the prayer closet.

277
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:13,800
And they're not here because we let the busyness of life keep us from investing in the thing that we've been invited to invest in this whole time.

278
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:16,800
And then we say things like nobody knows us and we're alone.

279
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:22,800
And the reality is we have to invest in these relationships when things are fine, when things are normal.

280
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:26,800
So that when things are hard, they are here for us.

281
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:34,800
When we're in the regular rhythms of life, it can be so easy to neglect spiritual community.

282
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:42,800
But if we neglect building it when things are good, we won't have it when things...

283
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:44,800
I wrote this in my notes.

284
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:46,800
Fit hits the shan.

285
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:48,800
Yeah?

286
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:49,800
Okay.

287
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:55,800
And as a pastor, I can tell you from experience, from counseling sessions with people,

288
00:26:55,800 --> 00:26:59,800
that Satan does some of his best work when he can get us alone and suffering.

289
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:04,800
When we can be experiencing sorrow and isolated from the community.

290
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:11,800
And so we have to, as we go through suffering, and it's hard.

291
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,800
It's hard to be vulnerable.

292
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:14,800
It's hard to be transparent.

293
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:15,800
It's hard to acknowledge pain.

294
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:20,800
We'd rather just create a fake social media post that makes it look like we're going to make it through.

295
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:24,800
We need to be in community with one another.

296
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:27,800
Hebrews 3 says it this way:

297
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:34,800
"See to it, brothers and sisters, that none of you has a sinful, unbelieving heart that turns away from the living God.

298
00:27:34,800 --> 00:27:41,800
But encourage one another daily, as long as it is called today, so that none of you will be hardened by sin's deceitfulness."

299
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:44,800
I often think about this as like sin, like temptation.

300
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:51,800
But I think it's also the sorrows, the brokenness of the life that we live on earth.

301
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:55,800
And sorrow has a way of hardening our hearts towards God's goodness.

302
00:27:55,800 --> 00:28:00,800
And so it says, "Meet with one another daily, encourage one another, so that when sorrow comes, when pain comes,

303
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:03,800
you can remind each other that this isn't the end of the story.

304
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:09,800
We need spiritual community that becomes like family, so that when sorrow comes, we don't become overcome by it.

305
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:14,800
Believing the lies from the enemy that harden our heart to the redemptive work that God is doing."

306
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:25,800
This spiritual truth is backed up by modern science.

307
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:29,800
In his teaching on this that some of you will watch in your small groups this week,

308
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:35,800
John Mark Homer quotes a study done on people who went through significant traumatic events.

309
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:41,800
And the scientists were trying to figure out that all of us have seen people that went through traumatic events

310
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:47,800
and some people come out on the other end stronger, better, like more whole as a human being,

311
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:52,800
and other people like let it destroy their lives and crash the plane and burn out, right?

312
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:57,800
And so they were doing this study on these people who had significant trauma in their lives,

313
00:28:57,800 --> 00:28:59,800
and they were trying to figure out what is the difference?

314
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:03,800
What is the thing that makes some people come out of it stronger, some people learn and grow,

315
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:06,800
and other people crash the plane.

316
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:10,800
They had their theories, they had their hypothesis, which turned out to be wrong,

317
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:15,800
and what they came up with is that for those people that had a relational home for their pain,

318
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:22,800
they were the ones who were most likely to come out of traumatic events on the other end stronger and better for it.

319
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:28,800
This is biblical truth expressed in science.

320
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:34,800
We need one another to carry the burdens of this broken world.

321
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:37,800
I love how Comer summarizes this section in his teaching.

322
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:41,800
He says, "If Jesus needs a few friends to bear the weight of the cross,

323
00:29:41,800 --> 00:29:45,800
how much more do we need each other to bear our crosses?"

324
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:51,800
Jesus, fully human and fully God, weeping in the garden,

325
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:55,800
with Peter, James, and John, supposed to be weeping with him instead falling asleep.

326
00:29:55,800 --> 00:29:58,800
We might have time to get to that, I'm not sure.

327
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:04,800
If Jesus needs people, how much more do we?

328
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:11,800
And if you're anything like me, you probably like the idea of this message.

329
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:18,800
But the execution is hard.

330
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:21,800
And I think most of us are a lot like the disciples.

331
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:27,800
The spirit is willing, but the flesh is weak.

332
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:36,800
As you lean into community, as you seek to go past spiritual platitudes and small talk,

333
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:42,800
it will be difficult and the enemy will whisper a thousand excuses in your ear for why you shouldn't get vulnerable,

334
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:46,800
for why you shouldn't be transparent, for why you shouldn't share what's going on in your life,

335
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:50,800
for why you shouldn't point out to somebody else what you see God doing in their life.

336
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:55,800
There will be a million excuses and it will be far easier just to say,

337
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:58,800
"Weather looks good out there for the next week, doesn't it?

338
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:01,800
How's your fantasy football team doing?"

339
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:04,800
Right?

340
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:06,800
It will always be easier to do that.

341
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:15,800
Spirit is willing, but the flesh is weak.

342
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:21,800
As I was writing that section of my message, I reminded, I told you,

343
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:24,800
I've been working on developing a community like this.

344
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:25,800
It's not easy.

345
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:26,800
It takes time.

346
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:32,800
I was reminded of this evening that some of my spiritual community had gotten together

347
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:37,800
and one of the people in the community suggested that we get vulnerable and transparent,

348
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:39,800
that we share some things that have been going on,

349
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:40,800
some things that we've been wrestling with,

350
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:41,800
some things we've been holding on to.

351
00:31:44,800 --> 00:31:49,800
And the person suggested it and then a week went by and we came together

352
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:52,800
and it came to that point where it was going to be the time for us to do it.

353
00:31:52,800 --> 00:31:55,800
And the person who had suggested it said,

354
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:57,800
"I changed my mind.

355
00:31:57,800 --> 00:31:58,800
Let's not do this."

356
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:05,800
The Spirit is willing.

357
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,800
The flesh is weak.

358
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:11,800
It's like we want to do it, but, oh man, it's going to be so hard.

359
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:17,800
And we all, we pushed through it and we all took turns and we all shared.

360
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:22,800
And the person whose idea it was kept,

361
00:32:22,800 --> 00:32:25,800
"Nah, I'll go last, I'll go last, I'll go last."

362
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:28,800
And then there was no more people to go.

363
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:29,800
It was their turn.

364
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:33,800
And they were like, "Hmm, maybe next week."

365
00:32:33,800 --> 00:32:38,800
And I watched this person.

366
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:42,800
I watched him overcome all of the lies of the enemy that said,

367
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:44,800
"Don't get vulnerable with these people.

368
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:46,800
Don't share with them what you're going through.

369
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:48,800
Don't share with them this thing that you've been carrying."

370
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:53,800
Shame, fear, lies from the enemy.

371
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:56,800
And I watched this person by the power of the Spirit,

372
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:59,800
through the trembling of their lips,

373
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:01,800
get out this thing that they've been holding on to.

374
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:05,800
And I just watched freedom break through.

375
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:08,800
Grace be extended.

376
00:33:08,800 --> 00:33:14,800
We need each other to carry our burdens.

377
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:19,800
We need each other in the joy and in the sorrow.

378
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:22,800
So the application for this week is real easy.

379
00:33:22,800 --> 00:33:26,800
It's just a little bit from last week added on to.

380
00:33:26,800 --> 00:33:29,800
Get around the table with some brothers and sisters in Christ.

381
00:33:29,800 --> 00:33:30,800
Share a meal together.

382
00:33:31,800 --> 00:33:34,800
And don't settle for small talk or spiritual platitudes.

383
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:35,800
Share a joy and a sorrow.

384
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:38,800
Share a high and a low from the weak.

385
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:41,800
Encourage one another and pray for one another.

386
00:33:41,800 --> 00:33:46,800
This is small little baby steps that over time will have compounding interest.

387
00:33:47,800 --> 00:33:53,800
I stole the wording of this from a pastor.

388
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:54,800
I loved how he said it.

389
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:56,800
He said, "Trade shallow for honest."

390
00:33:56,800 --> 00:34:00,800
And he quoted his worship pastor.

391
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:03,800
John Mark Homer talks about highs and lows in his teaching.

392
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:05,800
Share a high and a low from the weak.

393
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:08,800
The worship pastor at this guy's church had one that was even better.

394
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,800
I love this.

395
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:13,800
Share a nope, a dope, and a hope.

396
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:17,800
Like this past week, what was like nope?

397
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:19,800
What was dope?

398
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:22,800
And what do we have hope for in the coming week?

399
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:27,800
Trade shallow for honest and trade comparison for compassion.

400
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:35,800
We're going to be tempted when somebody that's in our community brings something that they want to celebrate to us.

401
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:39,800
The flesh in us is going to be tempted to compare their joy with our joy.

402
00:34:40,800 --> 00:34:45,800
To covet, to do all kinds of nasty, sinful stuff.

403
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:49,800
Stop comparing your story to their story and just be present with them.

404
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:54,800
Celebrate what God's doing in their life and sit with them in the sorrows and brokenness of this world.

405
00:34:54,800 --> 00:35:05,800
All right, as we land the plane here, I want to make sure that we see the main thing that connects both Christ's joy and his sorrow in these passages.

406
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:08,800
Because I think it's important.

407
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:14,800
I think it's important that we remind ourselves why we're putting an emphasis on Christian community.

408
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:20,800
We should absolutely love and invest in relationships with people outside the faith.

409
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,800
We should love our neighbors.

410
00:35:22,800 --> 00:35:24,800
We should invest in our coworkers.

411
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:33,800
But the reason that we prioritize Christian community is because we, as followers of Jesus, interpret the circumstances of this broken world the same way.

412
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:40,800
We need to remind ourselves of what's actually happening, of the spiritual realities behind the physical realities.

413
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:45,800
And that's what we see in this passage.

414
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:53,800
I'm going to read both and just see if you find one particular thing that is present.

415
00:35:54,800 --> 00:36:03,800
While they were eating, Jesus took bread and when he had given thanks, he broke it and he gave it to his disciples saying, "Take, this is my body."

416
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:09,800
I'm going to give you guys a hint because it might be harder than I thought it was going to be.

417
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:10,800
Okay?

418
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:11,800
Just pay attention.

419
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:19,800
Then he took a cup and when he had given thanks, he gave it to them and they all drank from it.

420
00:36:19,800 --> 00:36:21,800
The center of Christ's joy.

421
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:30,800
Later, going a little farther, he fell to the ground and he prayed, "If possible this hour might pass from him, Abba, Father."

422
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:32,800
He said, "Everything is possible for you.

423
00:36:32,800 --> 00:36:36,800
Take this cup from me.

424
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:40,800
Yet not what I will, but what you will."

425
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,800
Both at the center of Christ's joy and his suffering is a cup.

426
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:45,800
They're different cups.

427
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:51,800
There's spiritual realities behind the physical realities.

428
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:56,800
The suffering that Jesus is about to experience is a result of all of humanity's rebellion towards God.

429
00:36:56,800 --> 00:37:02,800
It is the cup of God's wrath that Jesus will receive on our behalf.

430
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:10,800
And as followers of Jesus, we realize that all suffering, every suffering that we experience on earth is somehow a result of sin.

431
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:15,800
It's either our sin, others' sin, or the unintended consequences of a broken world.

432
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:23,800
And so when we come in contact with sorrow as Christians, we remind ourselves that this is not God's will for our lives.

433
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:30,800
That this is, in some way, the brokenness of this world being played out.

434
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:43,800
So we encourage one another daily, not to be hardened by the lies of sin, but to put our hope in Christ, whose heel was bruised, but who crushed the head of the serpent through his resurrection.

435
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:48,800
All sorrow and suffering is but a vapor compared to the eternal glory we are awaiting in Christ Jesus.

436
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:55,800
Not only is there a cup at the center of Christ's suffering, but there is a cup at the center of his joy.

437
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:57,800
And that is the cup of God's blessing, his grace.

438
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:02,800
Just like followers of Jesus know that all suffering is rooted in sin.

439
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:06,800
We know that all joy that we experience is rooted in God's grace.

440
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:07,800
That's all a gift.

441
00:38:08,800 --> 00:38:10,800
And this is why we have to remind ourselves.

442
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:17,800
We have to come around Christian community because it's a very big temptation for us to get that raise at work and say, "Man, did I work hard for that."

443
00:38:17,800 --> 00:38:20,800
It's a gift.

444
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:24,800
The breath in your lungs is a gift.

445
00:38:24,800 --> 00:38:34,800
Every joy that we experience on earth is a gift from God that we did not earn and we do not deserve, and yet he freely gives it to us.

446
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:44,800
James 1, "Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of the heavenly lights, who does not change like shifting shadows."

447
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:52,800
He chose to give us birth through the word of truth that we might be a kind of first fruits of all that he created.

448
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:58,800
Eventually, all creation will catch up to this reality that every good and perfect thing is a gift from God.

449
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:02,800
But right now, we are the first fruits of that reality.

450
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:06,800
So we root our joy in the reality that it is a gift from God.

451
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:12,800
Poor David.

452
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:18,800
I don't think David sang yet at church.

453
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:22,800
And of course, I asked him to sing a solo by himself at the end of the service.

454
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,800
So be gracious, right?

455
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:26,800
Love on David.

456
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:34,800
I want to conclude today's message with a new song that I think handles this tension well.

457
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:37,800
Worship songs are all about joy, right?

458
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:39,800
We love to sing happy songs.

459
00:39:40,800 --> 00:39:45,800
And sometimes we sing sad songs, but rarely are there songs that carry the tension of both.

460
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:55,800
And I listened to the song recently and I love it because the one verse says, "If your life's been resurrected by the war that Jesus won, praise the Lord."

461
00:39:56,800 --> 00:40:01,800
And the next verse says, "For the one who's brokenhearted and it's hard to sing this song."

462
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:05,800
And that is what Christian community is all about.

463
00:40:06,800 --> 00:40:11,800
There are people in this room who have stories and testimonies of God's resurrection power this morning.

464
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:17,800
We got people like Joe coming in here and saying, "Let me tell you a story about a girl who thought she had no worth."

465
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:24,800
And how Jesus resurrected those dry bones and made life again.

466
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:26,800
We've got those stories in here.

467
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:37,800
And we also have stories of loss of job, of miscarriage, of diagnosis, of whatever it might be.

468
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:44,800
There are joy and sorrow in here and we need to remind ourselves that the sorrow is temporary and won't last forever.

469
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,800
We need to remind ourselves that joy is a gift from God.

470
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:59,800
May we be a church that intentionally forms Christian family around a table that isn't shallow or built on spiritual platitudes,

471
00:40:59,800 --> 00:41:04,800
but that fights to defiantly celebrate joy and intentionally carry one another's sufferings.

